#!/usr/bin/env bash
# screenshot — Wayland/Hyprland screen capture with optional tensaku annotation.
#
# Usage: screenshot <region|full|clipboard|text|qr> [--annotate]
#   region     drag-select a region (screen frozen during selection if
#              hyprpicker is present, so you capture exactly what you saw)
#   full       the active monitor
#   clipboard  annotate whatever image is currently on the clipboard
#              (always annotates; result goes back to the clipboard)
#   text       drag-select a region and copy its text (OCR with tesseract)
#   qr         drag-select a region and copy the QR code it holds (zbarimg)
#
# region/full: capture -> save to ~/Pictures AND copy to the clipboard; with
# --annotate, hand off to tensaku (annotate -> back to the clipboard).
# text/qr save nothing: the image stays in memory and only the decoded result
# reaches the clipboard. --annotate does not apply to them.
#
# Bound from dotfiles/.config/hypr/bindings.lua (the Print family); bare Print
# opens flameshot.
#
# The text and qr modes are adapted from Omarchy's omarchy-capture-text and
# omarchy-capture-qr, under their license:
#
